                        "entry_id": "291e56f1-1240-3ffa-8987-de82f7bdf281",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The mesentery that attaches the sigmoid colon to the posterior abdominal wall."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "544a16fd-815d-4205-88d7-41c360181f91",
                                "sense_id": "71e5a6cb-d01d-3e54-a65b-e55efb425a2f",
                                "text": "I designate this duplicature of peritoneum as Gruber's fold, because so far as I am aware, Gruber was the first to describe it. It controls to some extent the mesosigmoid and sustains it .from prolapse especially keeping it out of the pelvis."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a776bd49-1f97-4c29-b607-a8b0af708ceb",
                                "sense_id": "71e5a6cb-d01d-3e54-a65b-e55efb425a2f",
                                "text": "This places the reflection under stretch and facilitates its division. (c) The reflection and underlying mesosigmoidal fascia have been retracted to the left and the mesosigmoid to the right."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "aed8d4fc-7c53-4050-b9a0-a6567cf025c1",
                                "sense_id": "71e5a6cb-d01d-3e54-a65b-e55efb425a2f",
                                "text": "The inferior mesenteric artery and vein are exposed by retracting the mesosigmoid to the left (by the assistant)."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
